  "worked_solution": "To find the GCF, we list the factors of the coefficients and identify any common variable factors in the expressions.\n\nThe factors of $12$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,6,\\,12.\n$$\n\nThe factors of $18$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,6,\\,9,\\,18.\n$$\n\nThe common factors of $12$ and $18$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,6.\n$$\n\nThe greatest of these common factors is $6.$\n\nNow we look at the variable factors. Since $12$ has no variable and $18z$ contains $z,$ there are no variable factors in common.\n\nThus, the greatest common factor of $12$ and $18z$ is $6.$",
